      path: "reference/races.transformations/animals/race.md",
      text: "Animals\r\n\r\n[center][img]https://images-ext-1.discordapp.net/external/FOK39T7mQRHsx0JJvlXLiZWEwmoPpdXuzJR88qdMgLY/http/oi68.tinypic.com/2eyg75g.jpg[/img][/center][hr]\r\nSkin Color: Varies depending on species \r\nAppearance: Any animal species from Earth, sometimes anthropomorphic \r\nPlanet of Origin: Earth\r\nBiography: While 'Animals' is certainly a generic term for a range of species, in this instance it refers to the unique Animals of Earth who have taken anthropomorphic qualities. Capable of speech and bi-pedal movement in some cases, these Animals live amongst the Humans in their daily lives, with all the sentience of their Earth neighbors. For some unknown reason, Animals have an inherent ability to shapeshift that goes ignored and undoable by some through sheer lack of practice, but many have taken classes with the infamous Shapeshifting School to learn to temper this ability. With this ability they are able to transform their appearance into that of nearly anything depending on their skill level, including other races.\r\n\r\nSTARTING ITEMS[hr]\r\n[list][*] First Aid Kit x2\r\n[*]Senzu Leaf[/list]\r\n\r\nRACIAL TRAITS\r\n[hr]\r\nPupil of The Shapeshifting School - At the start of a match, you may copy one Racial Trait of an opponent's race.\r\n\r\nTrue Companion - Your quests take 1/2 of the listed WPD. Your Joint Quests take an additional -100 WPD, to a minimum of 100 WPD. \r\n\r\nCLASSES\r\n[hr]\r\nShapeshifting School Star Pupil - At the start of a match, you may copy all of the Racial Traits of an opponent's race. If that race allows them to choose the RACIAL TRAITS of another race other than your own, you must copy whatever they have chosen. \r\n\r\nBirds of A Feather -  Your Bukujutsu is considered one higher for all effects and purposes.This does not count towards the 2 level gap for specializations. When performing an attack that requires Bukujutsu, the attack gains +2 to the results. You may spend +1 KI Point before attacking to have that attack unable to be BLOCKED.\r\n\r\nWild Animal - Your single dice attacks do +(10% Power) Damage for every SUCCESSFUL single dice attack you have performed prior to that attack to a maximum of +(30% Power) Damage. This damage resets when one of your single dice attacks is STOPPED.\r\n\r\nNatural Camouflage - Whenever your defensive roll result is 10 or more higher than your opponent's attack roll result, your next attack can use result modifications to CRITICAL. You may have your opponent reroll their defensive roll against that attack, but must accept the second roll.\n",
